All done. Here's what I added:

**`txtar/archive.go`** — new method after the `File` type:

```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false if no such file exists.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	for i := range a.Files {
		if a.Files[i].Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```

Note: I used index-based range (`for i := range a.Files`) and return `&a.Files[i]` rather than `&f` from a value range, so the caller gets a pointer into the actual archive storage (allowing mutations to be visible).

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — `TestArchiveLookup` covering both outcomes (found and not found). All tests pass.

